[Music]  Bayesian - Oh our pure natural  refreshing mineral water comes from the  ancient river stats best of all a bottle  of Bayesian 200 has 200 milligrams of  Bayesian mineral that four to five  doctors believe reduces the risk of  addition Alice Jimmy goes to the grocery  store Bayes Mart to buy some water he  wonders what the company means when they  say a bottle of Bayesian 200 has 200  milligrams of Bayesian it's that on  average could it vary a lot by bottle  and how many doctors were surveyed and  how can they distinguish correlation  from causation hmm  sources faysville continued operas and  or discrete town are there major  differences between these sources three  segments of the stats River are used as  sources for Bayesian 201 in Bayes ville  one in continue Appa less and one in  discrete town  the average Bayesian level is different  for these three sources on average a  bottle source from Bayes Ville has 250  milligrams of Bayesian bottle from  continued Oppel us has a hundred and  ninety milligrams and a bottle from  discrete town has 160 milligrams even  within each of these sources there is  variation for a random bottle how much  Bayesian do you expect it to contain is  it the simple average 200 milligrams a  it is the simple average B it's more  than the simple average C it's less than  the simple average or D it depends as in  so many other situations the answer is  that it depends  the average Bayesian level is a weighted  average of the separate average Bayesian  levels for the three cities where the  weights depend on what proportion of  water is sourced from each of the cities  the simple average makes sense if  one-third of the water comes from each  of the cities  but if for example 2/3 of the water  comes from discrete town and only  one-sixth comes from Bay's ville and 1/6  from continue Appa less then the overall  average is 180 milligrams in general let  Y be the Bayesian content of a random  water bottle and B C and D be the events  that the water in the bottle comes from  Bay's ville continuous and discrete town  respectively then the overall average is  a weighted average of the separate  averages the expected value of y is e of  Y given B P of B plus e of y given C P  of C plus e of Y given D P of D let X be  a random variable that indicates which  city the water comes from say with x  equals 1 meaning Bayes Ville X equals 2  meaning continued appleís and x equals 3  meaning discrete town the above identity  can be expressed even more compactly as  a of y equals e of a of Y given X this  identity is known as iterated  expectation or Adams law  Jimmy is also concerned about how much  the Bayesian content varies by bottle  not just the average amount in a bottle  suppose that a bottle is equally likely  to be sourced from each of the three  cities for each source water bottles  have a standard deviation of 10  milligrams in their Bayesian content  what is the overall standard deviation  of Bayesian content in a random water  bottle a 10 milligrams be more than 10  milligrams C less than 10 milligrams or  D it depends is the overall variance the  weighted average of the three separate  variances  we can answer Jimmy's question visually  if the answer is yes then moving a  cities pile will not change the overall  standard deviation but in general the  overall standard deviation does change  when we move a pile even though we are  not changing the separate standard  deviations the key is that there are two  types of variation the Bayesian content  varies within each city and it also  varies between cities remarkably we can  get the overall variance simply by  adding these two contributions the  variance of y is e of the variance of Y  given X plus the variance of e of Y  given X the first term is the average of  the separate variances for each city the  second term is the variance between the  separate averages for each city this  identity is known as eaves law in this  example the variance of Y given X is 100  since within each city the variance is  100 and a of Y given X is 250 if x  equals 1 190 if x equals 2 and 160 if x  equals 3 which gives that the variance  of e of Y given X is 1400 by eaves law  the variance of Y is 100 plus 1400 which  is 1500 the standard deviation is the  square root of this variance which is  about 40 milligrams this is much higher  than 10 milligrams just using the  average of the three separate variances  ignores the second term in eves law  Jimny is right to be skeptical and to  seek more refined data with multiple  sources of water there are multiple  sources of variation  [Music]  you

